        "id": "one-list-two-names",
        "kind": "explain",
        "blocks": [],
        "headline": "b = a gives the same list a second name, and append changes that one list in place.",
        "lead": [
          {
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "text": "Assignment never copies a list. After b = a, both names lead to one list, so a change through either name shows through both. a.copy() builds a new list instead."
          },
          {
            "kind": "callout",
            "tone": "key",
            "text": "Two names, one list. Use copy when you need two lists."
          }
        ],
        "reveal": [],
        "introducesTerms": [
          "alias"
        ],
        "visualStateId": "",
        "checkQuestionId": "python-lists-and-tuples-alias-check",
